+Watch out: the page must load the Symbols font itself (the demo adds a `<link>`); without it icons fall back to Material Icons, which has the same names for the common glyphs. `.fig-select` behaves via `FigSelect.install()` (`tokens/FigSelect.js`): a row click sets the trigger text, marks `aria-selected`, closes and fires a bubbling `fig-select` event (`detail.value`); outside click and Escape close; Arrow keys move, Enter picks; one open at a time. It reuses `ux/Menu`'s native-`<details>` recipe but with delegated listeners, so plain markup works with no per-instance setup. **Phone sheet (DS 2.6 C):** under 600 px of screen width the open panel is a bottom sheet over a 40% scrim, pure CSS in `tokens.css` plus one line in `FigSelect.js` (a tap on the scrim, which is the `<details>` itself, closes it). Not `ux/Popover`: that anchors a JS-built box to a trigger, and the select is native `<details>` with delegated listeners, so adopting it would mean rebuilding the markup. The sheet is by screen width, not the `.fig-mobile` class, and does not work inside a `.fig-lay` (its container-type traps `position: fixed`). The 264 cap and scroll are CSS.
